w who much does a policeman make in the US, please enlighten me.<br /> <br /> My dad lives in a diferent &quot;provincia&quot; (sort of like states in the U.S. but less autonomus) and he told me people there are taking the streets armed against the mobs, its crazy, but Argentina is a country of survivors above all else, we'll make it out of this... and it will probably happen again in ten years give or take... sigh....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/122-talum","name":"Talum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar122_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T17:06:48-08:00","id":27624,"title":"","content":"I don't know exactly, but I'm certain it's more than $1000 a month.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They call me... Mr. Demmywinks.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1210-demetrius7997","name":"Demetrius7997","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T17:18:20-08:00","id":27633,"title":"","content":"And most of them are unionized...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:00:19-08:00","id":27644,"title":"","content":"Stay safe, I'm hoping for the best and that you're okay","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T18:02:38-08:00","id":27645,"title":"","content":"All of the police in the US are unionized. But part of the contracts always written is that they aren't allowed to strike. I believe the starting salary for most is over $50k a year. And this doesn't include any additional work they can legally acquire, or bonuses and perks that come with the job. And this is just the local police for any city or town. State police might be paid significantly more, depending on the state. I believe that the New Jersey State Police for example has a starting salary over $62k/yr. However, one of the requirements for that job is a Bachelor's degree, and prior military service is also looked for. And the physical requirements are somewhat arduous. (Knew some people that said it was harsh. First thing they do is put you in a boxing ring with a 6' 6&quot; monster, at least that's what they did then)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T06:47:10-08:00","id":31619,"title":"","content":"Talum, where are you, C\u00f3rdoba? I was in Buenos Aires when you posted and I got wind of the news, but I had no problems there.<br /> <br /> I hope things are back to normal. Argentina is a great country, I've visited three times in the last five years, and I've loved it every time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1714-the-butcher","name":"The Butcher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T11:55:02-08:00","id":31815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/26760-my-city-and-country-to-an-extent-has-gone-sabbat?p=27645#post27645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the police in the US are unionized. But part of the contracts always written is that they aren't allowed to strike. I believe the starting salary for most is over $50k a year. And this doesn't include any additional work they can legally acquire, or bonuses and perks that come with the job. And this is just the local police for any city or town. State police might be paid significantly more, depending on the state. I believe that the New Jersey State Police for example has a starting salary over $62k/yr. However, one of the requirements for that job is a Bachelor's degree, and prior military service is also looked for. And the physical requirements are somewhat arduous. (Knew some people that said it was harsh. First thing they do is put you in a boxing ring with a 6' 6&quot; monster, at least that's what they did then)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering how morbidly obese some of the police men in America are, I'm inclined to believe that in some areas the in-career physical requirements are more or less hand-waved to have enough Police men in force.<br /> <br /> Now when it comes to Argentina, I'm not sure about the medium salary but 1000$ month sounds almost ridiculously low even for a well developed and wealthy south American country where living costs are (still) much less than say north America or Europe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T14:19:27-08:00","id":31890,"title":"","content":"God this is crazy I hope you will be safe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64